{"title":"Career roadmap · Mining Geologist","role":"Mining Geologist","summary":"A Mining Geologist applies geology to the exploration, evaluation, extraction and management of mineral resources. The role covers geological mapping, mineral identification, drilling, core logging, sampling, grade control, ore-body modelling, resource estimation and mine production support.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Sc. (Bachelor of Science – General / Honours)","Course":"Geology / Earth Science"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"This is a directly aligned career for a Geology / Earth Science graduate. However, for many professional geologist positions, especially specialist and long-term roles, an M.Sc. in Geology / Applied Geology / Economic Geology can substantially improve career options."},{"type":"h","text":"Career-route check"},{"type":"note","label":"Starts","text":"Year 1"},{"type":"note","label":"Current degree","text":"B.Sc. Geology / Earth Science"},{"type":"note","label":"Desired career","text":"Mining Geologist"},{"type":"flow","items":["Geology","Mineral Exploration","Mining","Resource Management"],"label":"Career cluster"},{"type":"note","label":"Entry accessibility","text":"Direct/near-direct"},{"type":"note","label":"Typical entry titles","text":"Geology Trainee, Junior Geologist, Mining Geologist, Mine Geologist, Exploration Geologist, Grade Control Geologist"},{"type":"note","label":"Assumption","text":"three/four-year B.Sc. structure depending on the university, beginning in 2026."}]},{"heading":"Career horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career direction"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"Build geology, mineralogy, petrology, field mapping, economic geology, GIS and exploration fundamentals."}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"Enter exploration/mine geology and develop skills in drilling, logging, sampling, grade control and geological modelling."}],[{"text":"2035–2040"},{"text":"Progress toward Senior Geologist, Resource Geologist, Mine Geologist or Exploration Specialist."}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"Move toward Principal Geologist, Chief Geologist, Exploration Manager, Resource Manager or Technical Services leadership."}]]}]},{"heading":"What to build each year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["When","Build this","Learn from","Proof of progress","Gap it moves"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1 Sem 1"},{"text":"Physical geology, minerals, rocks and Earth processes"},{"text":"NPTEL","url":"https://nptel.ac.in/"},{"text":"Mineral/rock identification portfolio"},{"text":"Geological foundation"}],[{"text":"Year 1 Sem 2"},{"text":"Mineralogy, crystallography and petrology"},{"text":"University laboratory + fieldwork"},{"text":"Mineral and rock report"},{"text":"Materials knowledge"}],[{"text":"Year 2 Sem 1"},{"text":"Structural geology, stratigraphy and geomorphology"},{"text":"NPTEL + field mapping"},{"text":"Geological map"},{"text":"Mapping capability"}],[{"text":"Year 2 Sem 2"},{"text":"Economic geology and ore deposits"},{"text":"NPTEL + case studies"},{"text":"Ore-deposit study"},{"text":"Mining knowledge"}],[{"text":"Year 3 Sem 1"},{"text":"Mineral exploration, drilling and geological sampling"},{"text":"Industry + fieldwork"},{"text":"Exploration workflow"},{"text":"Exploration capability"}],[{"text":"Year 3 Sem 2"},{"text":"GIS, remote sensing, geostatistics and resource estimation"},{"text":"QGIS","url":"https://qgis.org/"},{"text":"Mineral-prospectivity map"},{"text":"Digital geology"}],[{"text":"Final Year / Sem 1"},{"text":"Grade control, core logging and mine operations"},{"text":"Mine/exploration internship"},{"text":"Drill-core/logging project"},{"text":"Industry readiness"}],[{"text":"Final Year / Sem 2"},{"text":"Dissertation + field project + PG/job preparation"},{"text":"Research/industry"},{"text":"Geological report"},{"text":"Career readiness"}]]},{"type":"h","tex